meta {
  name: Choose the payment method
  type: http
  seq: 10
  tags: [
    Customer_Cart
  ]
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v2/customer-cart/checkout/update
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "payment_method_id": "{{paymentMethodId}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data: isDefined
}

docs {
  Saves the address, payment method and the delivery method (with the pick-up point) of one package; omitted fields stay. Every value is checked against the current checkout: an unknown package — 404 on `package_id`; a method the package does not have — 422 on `delivery_method_id`; a point not in `customer-cart/pick-up-point/list` of the method or a point for a courier method — 422 on `pick_up_point_id`; a payment method not in `payment_methods` — 422 on `payment_method_id`; an address of another customer — 404 on `address_id`. The address is saved first: packages and methods depend on it. An address without an email gets the email of the customer; a guest passes it in the address. Order emails go to the email of the customer account (a guest gets none); SMS go to the phone of the address. Returns the recalculated checkout.
}
